bine vulnerability severities into one column (#3537)\n\nThis PR combines Critical, Important, Moderate, and Low severity CVE\ncounts into a single column (similar to Advisor Recommendations). We''re\nnot currently getting counts for Moderate and Low, so we''re filling them\nwith -- for now. With this, we have also removed the Total CVEs column.\nThe Vulnerabilities column is sorted by Critical CVEs until we get a\nspecial sort for the column from the backend. That means, if you include\nthe Critical column with the Vulnerabilities column, you''ll get a sort\non both columns. This is a temporary trade-off for the upcoming customer\ndemo.","tree":{"sha":"678df5188ccae4e48551a950abdf4e4ad999655b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/insights-inventory-frontend/git/trees/678df5188ccae4e48551a950abdf4e4ad999655b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/insights-inventory-frontend/git/commits/7bfe500f0e2a7448ebe760e310ea1ae366fe0767","verification":{"payload":"tree 678df5188ccae4e48551a950abdf4e4ad999655b\nparent 227bbc2c536f0315f71eacdb1f8cf03d7cd22c27\nauthor Michael Johnson <micjohns@redhat.com> 1788284672 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788284672 -0400\n\nfeat(RHINENG-30337): Combine vulnerability severities into one column (#3537)\n\nThis PR combines Critical, Important, Moderate, and Low severity CVE\ncounts into a single column (similar to Advisor Recommendations). We''re\nnot currently getting counts for Moderate and Low, so we''re filling them\nwith -- for now. With this, we have also removed the Total CVEs column.\nThe Vulnerabilities column is sorted by Critical CVEs until we get a\nspecial sort for the column from the backend. That means, if you include\nthe Critical column with the Vulnerabilities column, you''ll get a sort\non both columns. This is a temporary trade-off for the upcoming customer\ndemo.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlw8ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5gEQAGreA4Bpz8mQx