85,"sha":"363c7b20ec70c595c1dfd47125ad22a7249bbd9c"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"fbourasse","providerType":"User"},"email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-10T19:18:30Z","committedDate":"2026-04-10T19:18:30Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"fbourasse","providerType":"User"},"email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:22:51.755Z","repositoryId":142331085,"sha":"062ec86c95781ae7dae9094972973f7262c7a9cb"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"pvollenweider","providerType":"User"},"email":"pvollenweider@jahia.com","name":"Philippe Vollenweider"},"authoredDate":"2026-02-13T13:04:38Z","committedDate":"2026-02-13T13:04:38Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:22:51.755Z","repositoryId":142331085,"sha":"60cf853a86eb741dff33f3596c39529810fc928b"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:22:51.755Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/full-read-only-notifier/commits/a68fdff962b31745dbd6a13594bf2d45b7d5c6e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"SUPPORT-646: raise test coverage (JUnit 35→44, Jest 6→22, Cypress 4→10 specs, all green) (#22)\n\n* test: pin jsoup allowlist additions and characterize class/style wildcard bug (U6)\n\n- s/u tags, a[target|rel] additions each pinned individually\n- negative control: target stripped on non-anchor elements\n- characterization: .addAttributes(\"*\", ...) is a silent no-op (jsoup''s\n  all-tags pseudo-tag is \":all\"), so class/style are stripped today -\n  flagged for Stage 7 to fix and invert the assertion\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore: align package.json and AGENTS.md module version with pom.xml (2.0.5-SNAPSHOT)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: guard version consistency across pom.xml, package.json and AGENTS.md (D7)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: verify jsoup is embedded bundle-private and fix stale pom scope comment (D6)\n\n- pom-level guard (always runs): compile scope + Embed-Dependency jsoup;inline=true\n  + !org.jsoup.* in Import-Package\n- built-jar guard (skipped until mvn package): org/jsoup classes embedded,\n  manifest Import-Package free of org.jsoup\n- the jsoup dependency comment claimed provided scope keeps it off the bundle\n  classpath - reality is the opposite (embedded, bundle-private); comment fixed\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: characterize unsynchronized writeSettings race on concurrent first writes (U3)\n\nCyclicBarrier forces both threads through hasNode==false before either reaches\naddNode; asserts addNode fires twice (current racy behavior). Stage 7 must fix\nthe race and invert the assertion to times(1).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: pin admin route registration gating and permission wiring (F14)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: pin CKEditor5 MF-remote federation and inline Apollo client gotchas (D4, F16)\n\nAsserts against the RESOLVED ModuleFederationPlugin options (via\n@jahia/webpack-config''s helper), proving CKEditor5 is federated from\nrichtext-ckeditor5 - the opposite of AGENTS.md''s stale ''bundled locally'' gotcha.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: pin admin panel accessibility wiring (U5, Jest half)\n\n- live-region key remount (repeated identical messages re-announce)\n- aria-invalid/aria-errormessage wiring on both CKEditor view roots\n- distinct per-editor aria-labelledby, aria-required, aria-describedby\n- heading focus after loading resolves; cancel announcement\n- ckeditorReact mock upgraded: writer records attributes on the fake view\n  root and created editors are exposed via __getFakeEditors()\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): add shared helpers, default-message and edit-mode specs (F7, U8)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): add settings auto-publish and GraphQL schema-shape specs (U7, D1)\n\n- U7 resolves the Stage 2 reconciliation point: LIVE must pick up property\n  updates written by the mutation with no explicit publish (jmix:autoPublish)\n- D1 pins that the README''s flat root fields are dead (errors + null data,\n  message text deliberately not asserted) and the namespaced container\n  round-trips; includes an introspection cross-check\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): add fail-safe non-OFF banner branch and banner a11y specs (U9, U5)\n\nU9 uses PARTIAL read-only mode (readOnlyMode, not fullReadOnlyMode) as a real,\nreachable non-OFF status never set by the documented full toggle.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): pin dedupe cookie attributes - persistent ~1-day, not a session cookie (D3)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: pin Cypress spec inventory and reconcile AGENTS.md test docs (D5)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore: fix capitalized-comments lint nit in buildConfig.test.js\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): open API security profile post-import and re-aim legacy read-only spec\n\nTwo Stage 6 execution fixes, both verified against the live dockerized stack\n(final run: 10/10 specs, 43/43 tests green):\n\n- provisioning.yml: deploy security.profile=open AFTER the Digitall imports.\n  Raw stateless basic-auth GraphQL requests (cy.request) get ''Permission\n  denied'' on the jcr namespace and introspection under the default profile,\n  while browser-context cy.apollo calls pass - specs 07/08 need the open\n  profile. Placement matters: deploying the open profile before the imports\n  strips the provisioning API of the importSite operation and the Digitall\n  site silently never exists.\n\n- 09 spec: empirical Stage 6 finding - the legacy partial read-only switch\n  (maintenance.jsp?readOnlyMode=true) does NOT feed renderContext.readOnlyStatus\n  (only the full read-only controller writes it), so the planned partial-mode\n  lever for the fail-safe branch was unsound. Re-aimed as a characterization:\n  legacy partial mode does NOT trigger the notifier (with an off-banner\n  positive control so a missing component cannot fake the pass), literal OFF\n  renders no banner. The ''any non-OFF status warns'' JSP reading stays\n  documented, not asserted - no reachable third state exists single-node.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore: format helper module (line-width joins, type-literal wrap) - lint-clean\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: serialize writeSettings node creation to close concurrent first-write race (U3)\n\nThe hasNode -> addNode -> setProperty -> save() sequence ran unsynchronized,\nso two concurrent first writes for the same site could both observe\nhasNode == false and both call addNode (duplicate node or ItemExistsException\nat save). A class-level SETTINGS_WRITE_LOCK now serializes the check-create-\nsave window; the losing writer updates the winner''s node. Single JVM-wide\nlock is deliberate (rare admin-only writes); cluster-level races remain out\nof scope and are documented.\n\nThe U3 characterization test is inverted per its own handoff note: it now\npins the fixed contract (addNode exactly once, loser succeeds against the\nwinner''s node) with a serialization probe that fails deterministically if\nthe lock regresses.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: use jsoup '':all'' pseudo-tag so class/style are actually allowlisted (U6)\n\n.addAttributes(\"*\", ...) was a silent no-op - jsoup''s all-tags pseudo-tag is\n\":all\", a literal \"*\" only matches a tag actually named *. The documented\n''class/style allowed on every element'' rule (README Known Limitations) was\ntherefore never applied and both attributes were stripped at save and render\n(e.g. CKEditor Alignment output style=\"text-align:center\" was lost).\n\nSecurity note: the visitor-facing banner is unaffected as an XSS surface -\nthe render-time defense stack still applies (same jsoup allowlist re-applied\nat render, <c:out> escaping, and the client-side froSanitize() blocklist\nwhich strips style attributes/<style> elements before innerHTML injection),\nso inline styles are stored and round-tripped for the admin editor but never\nreach the public banner DOM.\n\nThe U6 characterization test is inverted per its own handoff note: it now\npins class and style preserved on any element.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"882e528cdceeff48696fa5323bfa8100604e2022","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/full-read-only-notifier/git/trees/882e528cdceeff48696fa5323bfa8100604e2022"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/full-read-only-notifier/git/commits/a68fdff962b31745dbd6a13594bf2d45b7d5c6e9","verification":{"payload":"tree 882e528cdceeff48696fa5323bfa8100604e2022\nparent d83bdb81829c6d13c4c1487b725f236c421c99f3\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784100472 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784100472 +0200\n\nSUPPORT-646: raise test coverage (JUnit 35→44, Jest 6→22, Cypress 4→10 specs, all green) (#22)\n\n* test: pin jsoup allowlist additions and characterize class/style wildcard bug (U6)\n\n- s/u tags, a[target|rel] additions each pinned individually\n- negative control: target stripped on non-anchor elements\n- characterization: .addAttributes(\"*\", ...) is a silent no-op (jsoup''s\n  all-tags pseudo-tag is \":all\"), so class/style are stripped today -\n  flagged for Stage 7 to fix and invert the assertion\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore: align package.json and AGENTS.md module version with pom.xml (2.0.5-SNAPSHOT)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: guard version consistency across pom.xml, package.json and AGENTS.md (D7)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: verify jsoup is embedded bundle-private and fix stale pom scope comment (D6)\n\n- pom-level guard (always runs): compile scope + Embed-Dependency jsoup;inline=true\n  + !org.jsoup.* in Import-Package\n- built-jar guard (skipped until mvn package): org/jsoup classes embedded,\n  manifest Import-Package free of org.jsoup\n- the jsoup dependency comment claimed provided scope keeps it off the bundle\n  classpath - reality is the opposite (embedded, bundle-private); comment fixed\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: characterize unsynchronized writeSettings race on concurrent first writes (U3)\n\nCyclicBarrier forces both threads through hasNode==false before either reaches\naddNode; asserts addNode fires twice (current racy behavior). Stage 7 must fix\nthe race and invert the assertion to times(1).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: pin admin route registration gating and permission wiring (F14)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: pin CKEditor5 MF-remote federation and inline Apollo client gotchas (D4, F16)\n\nAsserts against the RESOLVED ModuleFederationPlugin options (via\n@jahia/webpack-config''s helper), proving CKEditor5 is federated from\nrichtext-ckeditor5 - the opposite of AGENTS.md''s stale ''bundled locally'' gotcha.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: pin admin panel accessibility wiring (U5, Jest half)\n\n- live-region key remount (repeated identical messages re-announce)\n- aria-invalid/aria-errormessage wiring on both CKEditor view roots\n- distinct per-editor aria-labelledby, aria-required, aria-describedby\n- heading focus after loading resolves; cancel announcement\n- ckeditorReact mock upgraded: writer records attributes on the fake view\n  root and created editors are exposed via __getFakeEditors()\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): add shared helpers, default-message and edit-mode specs (F7, U8)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): add settings auto-publish and GraphQL schema-shape specs (U7, D1)\n\n- U7 resolves the Stage 2 reconciliation point: LIVE must pick up property\n  updates written by the mutation with no explicit publish (jmix:autoPublish)\n- D1 pins that the README''s flat root fields are dead (errors + null data,\n  message text deliberately not asserted) and the namespaced container\n  round-trips; includes an introspection cross-check\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): add fail-safe non-OFF banner branch and banner a11y specs (U9, U5)\n\nU9 uses PARTIAL read-only mode (readOnlyMode, not fullReadOnlyMode) as a real,\nreachable non-OFF status never set by the documented full toggle.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): pin dedupe cookie attributes - persistent ~1-day, not a session cookie (D3)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: pin Cypress spec inventory and reconcile AGENTS.md test docs (D5)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore: fix capitalized-comments lint nit in buildConfig.test.js\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): open API security profile post-import and re-aim legacy read-only spec\n\nTwo Stage 6 execution fixes, both verified against the live dockerized stack\n(final run: 10/10 specs, 43/43 tests green):\n\n- provisioning.yml: deploy security.profile=open AFTER the Digitall imports.\n  Raw stateless basic-auth GraphQL requests (cy.request) get ''Permission\n  denied'' on the jcr namespace and introspection under the default profile,\n  while browser-context cy.apollo calls pass - specs 07/08 need the open\n  profile. Placement matters: deploying the open profile before the imports\n  strips the provisioning API of the importSite operation and the Digitall\n  site silently never exists.\n\n- 09 spec: empirical Stage 6 finding - the legacy partial read-only switch\n  (maintenance.jsp?readOnlyMode=true) does NOT feed renderContext.readOnlyStatus\n  (only the full read-only controller writes it), so the planned partial-mode\n  lever for the fail-safe branch was unsound. Re-aimed as a characterization:\n  legacy partial mode does NOT trigger the notifier (with an off-banner\n  positive control so a missing component cannot fake the pass), literal OFF\n  renders no banner. The ''any non-OFF status warns'' JSP reading stays\n  documented, not asserted - no reachable third state exists single-node.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore: format helper module (line-width joins, type-literal wrap) - lint-clean\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: serialize writeSettings node creation to close concurrent first-write race (U3)\n\nThe hasNode -> addNode -> setProperty -> save() sequence ran unsynchronized,\nso two concurrent first writes for the same site could both observe\nhasNode == false and both call addNode (duplicate node or ItemExistsException\nat save). A class-level SETTINGS_WRITE_LOCK now serializes the check-create-\nsave window; the losing writer updates the winner''s node. Single JVM-wide\nlock is deliberate (rare admin-only writes); cluster-level races remain out\nof scope and are documented.\n\nThe U3 characterization test is inverted per its own handoff note: it now\npins the fixed contract (addNode exactly once, loser succeeds against the\nwinner''s node) with a serialization probe that fails deterministically if\nthe lock regresses.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: use jsoup '':all'' pseudo-tag so class/style are actually allowlisted (U6)\n\n.addAttributes(\"*\", ...) was a silent no-op - jsoup''s all-tags pseudo-tag is\n\":all\", a literal \"*\" only matches a tag actually named *. The documented\n''class/style allowed on every element'' rule (README Known Limitations) was\ntherefore never applied and both attributes were stripped at save and render\n(e.g. CKEditor Alignment output style=\"text-align:center\" was lost).\n\nSecurity note: the visitor-facing banner is unaffected as an XSS surface -\nthe render-time defense stack still applies (same jsoup allowlist re-applied\nat render, <c:out> escaping, and the client-side froSanitize() blocklist\nwhich strips style attributes/<style> elements before innerHTML injection),\nso inline styles are stored and round-tripped for the admin editor but never\nreach the public banner DOM.\n\nThe U6 characterization test is inverted per its own handoff note: it now\npins class and style preserved on any element.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVzZ4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB3gQAIIxIoUXfpA2bgdVdZh3v6DD\nfYWpikjH5A6k/3xpdTIjylradoVwib4aBvomtZYtvrJxBeEaYj3QvZLfEfo5y5qf\nSCvj+dKCMjz9uNR7pYdGuDFXUqskm0YyPYc6FZTeoG0zkNxPGKswbEyX8HdTHL0E\nq6xZf+fGI6JIZBCGHGqibuv+NUpnsS59Cm9PkBiCzVXlRphqL0HaZ5H21B6N31av\nmIoRwwL6c8no3RmQecqilWOhUS7z93yMsyyIzopz9OxmCqvD1fO/cIv5tWQDtpKC\nBN2ooXeBeLQTso2qxIGCeQthTzW2wxgvCUnJhFyznyktjuetpaVoim3Y8137+sd4\nFHgV+GVEJjbmGNOqQ5hgCf2uHpnTluT+upIpGSVDoD0kPsRhKx5scfSuxKkBh6sP\n7BHfli6/aJ0KH8AXbenMdGqoXPypLhmJ54NhUIm1vYptVnLBNOcAnavVVTsbRfc5\ni4nF9wtlL+pqgWYpQN6EDavwBDWG9s4d/5Bn1rCL+83sLS8prhzquArxuIN4HPj3\nR5QlTNYCswM9DU+i+7ZGosbBr2rK/54/OF6XMjB04AhdgTQp+cJHRsPc3KLfNfIz\nYgItkqvijVo4bh5Qwlgs3tyq9F1Icob4QGlS/MbBcuM0BhJfJOLEXIlu6hh0FOQZ\nI4HhtNyCB3Njx99Ik3nu\n=uFvv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T07:27:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type