rl":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/fbfba193ca8bce831a1a84aff21d36bb766062cc","node_id":"C_kwDOCMaeW9oAKGZiZmJhMTkzY2E4YmNlODMxYTFhODRhZmYyMWQzNmJiNzY2MDYyY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/230bd39fea43d95079c45e71fc637831dd851d20","sha":"230bd39fea43d95079c45e71fc637831dd851d20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/230bd39fea43d95079c45e71fc637831dd851d20"}],"sha":"fbfba193ca8bce831a1a84aff21d36bb766062cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/fbfba193ca8bce831a1a84aff21d36bb766062cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/230bd39fea43d95079c45e71fc637831dd851d20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T20:57:13Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T20:57:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix false ''IP address is unknown'' error during auto firmware update on restart (#1628)\n\n* Fix false ''IP address is unknown'' error during auto firmware update on restart\n\nOn adapter restart, onlineCheck() marks devices online via TCP ping before\nany MQTTClient has completed its async init (setIP is called after createObjects).\nfirmwareUpdate() already checked isOnline() but not getIP(), so it attempted\nan HTTP request with no IP address set, logging an error.\n\nAdded getIP() guard to firmwareUpdate() matching the pattern already used in\nhttpIoBrokerState(). The update is silently skipped (debug log) when the IP\nis not yet known; it will run in the next scheduled cycle (15 minutes) by\nwhich time the device will have fully reconnected.\n\nRefers to #1539\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix devices marked online too early during startup onlineCheck\n\nonlineCheck() runs at adapter startup and TCP-pings all known devices.\nIf a device responded to the ping it was immediately added to onlineDevices,\neven though the MQTT/CoAP protocol layer had not yet initialized (IP not set,\nobjects not created). This allowed premature actions like firmware update\nrequests against a device whose IP was still unknown.\n\nOn startup the online status is now only updated when a device is found\nto be unreachable (to clear stale online state). Positive ping results\nduring the startup run are ignored; each protocol layer sets online status\nitself once initialization is complete (MQTT: after setIP + deviceStatusUpdate,\nCoAP: same pattern). The subsequent periodic onlineCheck (60 s) resumes\nnormal behaviour including marking devices online.\n\nRefers to #1539\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix lint: add void to fire-and-forget deviceStatusUpdate call\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"17e7ab5c276fbdb56cd72e4e32f61d3f8ea6337d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/trees/17e7ab5c276fbdb56cd72e4e32f61d3f8ea6337d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/commits/230bd39fea43d95079c45e71fc637831dd851d20","verification":{"payload":"tree 17e7ab5c276fbdb56cd72e4e32f61d3f8ea6337d\nparent ad7d3e880dd7455f1a8c9f35100cb92d115e7370\nauthor Martin M. <mcm57@gmx.at> 1790283433 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790283433 +0200\n\nFix false ''IP address is unknown'' error during auto firmware update on restart (#1628)\n\n* Fix false ''IP address is unknown'' error during auto firmware update on restart\n\nOn adapter restart, onlineCheck() marks devices online via TCP ping before\nany MQTTClient has completed its async init (setIP is called after createObjects).\nfirmwareUpdate() already checked isOnline() but not getIP(), so it attempted\nan HTTP request with no IP address set, logging an error.\n\nAdded getIP() guard to firmwareUpdate() matching the pattern already used in\nhttpIoBrokerState(). The update is silently skipped (debug log) when the IP\nis not yet known; it will run in the next scheduled cycle (15 minutes) by\nwhich time the device will have fully reconnected.\n\nRefers to #1539\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix devices marked online too early during startup onlineCheck\n\nonlineCheck() runs at adapter startup and TCP-pings all known devices.\nIf a device responded to the ping it was immediately added to onlineDevices,\neven though the MQTT/CoAP protocol layer had not yet initialized (IP not set,\nobjects not created). This allowed premature actions like firmware update\nrequests against a device whose IP was still unknown.\n\nOn startup the online status is now only updated when a device is found\nto be unreachable (to clear stale online state). Positive ping results\nduring the startup run are ignored; each protocol layer sets online status\nitself once initialization is complete (MQTT: after setIP + deviceStatusUpdate,\nCoAP: same pattern). The subsequent periodic onlineCheck (60 s) resumes\nnormal behaviour including marking devices online.\n\nRefers to #1539\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix lint: add void to fire-and-forget deviceStatusUpdate call\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtY6pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALJAQAGfIzZU1n0FAj2+7Ocl/AlX3\n4wPUUFEwqXPktzatqL9eboHOFU/HsfHPRYwNQVSdWj9C/lWftGMX3KV6tDjYBklu\nzy/+Iz6d1TI5DF7UE2hWphjlDkYSB3HopYuvDJAjn+XBVDN+P/aB/qJRNLjyzMyW\nY5GhABrUZ7cec/dpqxZQi/+HwyaYBUUQAxfCJd31LvjQ2Zzrd0SnEgVoGHyfFjLL\nybHxO4IequjWEAkLn+TmNZWP/pMLbmpW1phbDoJLBiJW8lQSQXvSYEyL6csVELSt\ntMfcI8jNstUuSfJF0VNL2fpN09kHLpXPB+XI6OOUkYKLIiUtxFeoloxennZ3G5LV\nrhLF1T2f2JUMOlhYjYovMiq3IINpzjs82oHTGq4yYb7UF4ADIRjHE0CTUCcRP1JH\nmUK/zfdiv7ATWAyscp8ZmMWSMtzEso+r5aG3/bV0CbL1EK84snrAA73MTbYIuXFH\nUntAb9AFZOafOqdxMJAFN/1xV/4QJVJPRx4RhnJxNr3LCwN+L9HWSh/JqKalwW6n\nb+CtokgO29JjoisuNbDdOvCgoEnN9lO7yYPsH7rdETCkWKxdbLM1mBFHZi7orU4q\nfD6EDh5Y1k6sWQYr7+l7GVT6I0hygXmqRSPEVSf1tydJiGrdyUMuTwmxD5WNtTBL\ncghWJSowu+4lt37nhOe0\n=VpkQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T20:57:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/230bd39fea43d95079c45e71fc637831dd851d20","node_id":"C_kwDOCMaeW9oAKDIzMGJkMzlmZWE0M2Q5NTA3OWM0NWU3MWZjNjM3ODMxZGQ4NTFkMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/ad7d3e880dd7455f1a8c9f35100cb92d115e7370","sha":"ad7d3e880dd7455f1a8c9f35100cb92d115e7370","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/ad7d3e880dd7455f1a8c9f35100cb92d115e7370"}],"sha":"230bd39fea43d95079c45e71fc637831dd851d20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/230bd39fea43d95079c45e71fc637831dd851d20"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/ad7d3e880dd7455f1a8c9f35100cb92d115e7370/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T19:20:43Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T19:20:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Activate PLUG_UI LED control for plug devices with firmware >= 2.0.0 (#1624)\n\n* Activate PLUG_UI component for plug devices with firmware >= 2.0.0\n\n- Add firmware_version_min property to DeviceState to gate states on minimum firmware\n- Add isSemverAtLeast() filter in datapoints.ts / deleteNoDisplay() to remove states\n  whose firmware_version_min exceeds the connected device''s detected firmware version\n- Add deviceFirmwareVersion tracking to BaseClient (parseFirmwareSemver, setDeviceFirmwareVersion)\n  which parses the semver from strings like ''20250924-062655/1.7.1-gd336f31'', logs as debug,\n  and triggers object re-creation when PLUG_UI eligibility changes\n- On MQTT connect, set firmware version from Shelly.GetDeviceInfo fw_id response; re-evaluation\n  happens automatically whenever the version string is first received from the device\n- Uncomment addPlugsUI / addPlugpmUI calls in shellyplusplugs, shellyazplug, shellyplugmg3,\n  shellyplugpmg3, shellyplugsg3 — states are now filtered by firmware_version_min: ''2.0.0''\n- Add versionShort state to all devices (gen1 + gen2+) storing the parsed semver (e.g. ''1.7.1'')\n- Export addPlugsUI and addPlugpmUI from gen2-helper\n- Add translations for new state names\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update src-admin translations after npm run translate\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert admin/custom/ to master state (remove unrelated build artifacts)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix lint errors: add curly braces and parentheses for ESLint/prettier compliance\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update eslint.config.mjs\n\n* linter fixes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"97967ed781fd0ca80229468c64f20664494fe2ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/trees/97967ed781fd0ca80229468c64f20664494fe2ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/commits/ad7d3e880dd7455f1a8c9f35100cb92d115e7370","verification":{"payload":"tree 97967ed781fd0ca80229468c64f20664494fe2ed\nparent e2a7590d005e1f447f9b44c26c05e210db009379\nauthor Martin M. <mcm57@gmx.at> 1790191243 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790191243 +0200\n\nActivate PLUG_UI LED control for plug devices with firmware >= 2.0.0 (#1624)\n\n* Activate PLUG_UI component for plug devices with firmware >= 2.0.0\n\n- Add firmware_version_min property to DeviceState to gate states on minimum firmware\n- Add isSemverAtLeast() filter in datapoints.ts / deleteNoDisplay() to remove states\n  whose firmware_version_min exceeds the connected device''s detected firmware version\n- Add deviceFirmwareVersion tracking to BaseClient (parseFirmwareSemver, setDeviceFirmwareVersion)\n  which parses the semver from strings like ''20250924-062655/1.7.1-gd336f31'', logs as debug,\n  and triggers object re-creation when PLUG_UI eligibility changes\n- On MQTT connect, set firmware version from Shelly.GetDeviceInfo fw_id response; re-evaluation\n  happens automatically whenever the version string is first received from the device\n- Uncomment addPlugsUI / addPlugpmUI calls in shellyplusplugs, shellyazplug, shellyplugmg3,\n  shellyplugpmg3, shellyplugsg3 — states are now filtered by firmware_version_min: ''2.0.0''\n- Add versionShort state to all devices (gen1 + gen2+) storing the parsed semver (e.g. ''1.7.1'')\n- Export addPlugsUI and addPlugpmUI from gen2-helper\n- Add translations for new state names\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update src-admin translations after npm run translate\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert admin/custom/ to master state (remove unrelated build artifacts)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix lint errors: add curly braces and parentheses for ESLint/prettier compliance\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update eslint.config.mjs\n\n* linter fixes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtCaLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP3EQAI5gvXZRV86XY3jekevfTptP\nMBAa2+tndx3hFjLWinmuD/MzJ8ZCyncbb/0Tr23nWmOGoFpfnydKZk55RO+PGYf9\nYCUDPVVRsQ3wbGY/VcrSOi1OQaYT3Z0SqCKyoOpe32e1+6VSjvLvAF83yB6I/tv+\nLugqEFUcP1rFpINCSrjZpVw2qfTR87BLBKT6sLghs4mlRTHLK/rmZoQlkWufji93\n9KR8p7CpEjGhWv5p5AetA/FlLN8L+0u0iOn6CqYqLS2ZLVYB3U+z2wg8Tec/p4P3\nZ+ptZigfXmVDxIiI7r9RETKulb6tFCThsf6dHVAcuOqU7fDoL0TGJp6XwsZqkoTb\nVi6QQW/a7AFkbW1A6iBTM5o2B5526pbvMPuoOATiHbj3xcwI4CdQjCdKGzKaEdJw\nvoOjV3YkRToVBg3pKBJEYO01k5Bb4xCph2Khf2qAyzqvY3JNWjUhpctCR239kAPX\nODrGBTtuuBZy190WCL+TUpRZNlPyvQBtwkzlmC0Q7DxSti8OZxaVsCPckrHxqvZz\nkGhxi5dHf8/nF2ev4uruF3PwxCH9s+94euDaF2hK6Pr+SXsAPGAjWnKOh/I2DV7z\nZ3R53C+o1Be2wOUsZqZ+1F6D9neZRxXwlFNqfpeZL7UEKU/pCZkN5bV8/BO5QDd2\nwiZ6++SrVnOVoP3j9u47\n=bLny\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T19:20:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_