":"5199c1ee94e8f47e9fbfc7b2af2b0d99d762f575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/5199c1ee94e8f47e9fbfc7b2af2b0d99d762f575"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/84462479f0762ac79a87103f2f08adfa55338b8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T08:42:27Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T08:42:27Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"message":"chore: release v12.0.0\n\n- (@mcm1957) **BREAKING:** Adapter requires node.js >= 22, js-controller >= 7.7.2 and admin >= 8.0.11 now.\n- (@GermanBluefox) Codebase has been migrated to typescript.\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Duo Bulb E27 Gen 3 (shellyduobulbg3). [#1385]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Multicolor Bulb E27 Gen 3 (shellycolorblbg3). [#1386]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly 1L Gen4 (shelly1lg4) and Shelly 2L Gen4 (shelly2lg4).\n- (@mcm1957) Added experimental support for FrankEver Smart Sprinkler Controller (irrigation). [#1207]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Neo Smart Water Valve NAS-WV02W (neowatervalve). [#1322]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Top AC Portable EV Charger (topacportableevcharger) - **EXPERIMENTAL ONLY** [#1401]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Flood S Gen 4 (shellyfloodsg4). [#1380]\n- (@mcm1957) Added monophase mode support for Shelly 3EM G3 (shelly3em63g3). [#1540]\n- (@klein0r) Updated ble script (v1.4) for Shelly firmware > 2.0\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added a new \"Bluetooth map\" tab to the adapter configuration which shows which Bluetooth devices are received by which Shelly gateway, including the signal strength. The gateways are arranged in a circle and each device is shown at the gateway which receives it best - all other connections and the signal values can be switched on.\n- (@mcm1957) Added a \"BLE Map\" button to the device manager toolbar which opens the Bluetooth map.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The device tiles now show when a device was last seen, and a device which goes offline is marked as disconnected immediately instead of only after reloading the list.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The BLE gateway script can now be installed and updated from the device manager - per device or for all devices which already have it installed. The installed script version is shown in the device details.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The list of gateways which receive a Bluetooth device (state \"receivedBy\") now collects all gateways instead of showing only the receivers of the last message. A gateway which stops receiving a device is removed after one hour.\n- (@patricknitsch) Device Manager now automatically shows power values on the device tile, and voltage, current, energy and frequency in the device info, for any device that reports them.\n- (@mcm1957) The transition time can now be written for Shelly Dimmer1/Dimmer2 and for Gen2+ dimmers/lights (incl. Dimmer Gen3 and Dimmer Gen4). [#1214][#1224]\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed inverted Relay0.Switch state of Shelly 1L Gen3 (shelly1lg3), Shelly 1PM Mini Gen3 (shelly1pmminig3), Shelly Pro 2PM (shellypro2pm) and Shelly Plug S Gen3 (shellyplugsg3) caused by a device firmware bug. [#1318]\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed date states (timer/transition/boost start times) to report the timestamp in milliseconds so it is compatible with JavaScript Date handling.\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed authentication with Gen2+ devices running firmware 2.x which could fail with \"Wrong http username or http password!\" although the credentials were correct. [#1543]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed MQTT commands getting lost with \"mqtt prefix was not set\" if they were sent while a device was (re)connecting.\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed that the adapter needlessly rewrote object definitions on every device update and reconnect, which caused repeated object change events and log spam in other adapters (e.g. valuetrackerovertime). [#1560]\n- (@GermanBluefox) The device manager now updates the device list after renaming a device, after a firmware update and after installing the BLE gateway script - the cards showed outdated values before.\n- (@mcm1957) Added the missing translations for all datapoint names in all supported languages.\n- (@mcm1957) Added tests to validate that all datapoint names and descriptions are translated and that all i18n language files are consistent.\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed MQTT errors (\"Cannot read properties of undefined\") if a device closes the connection while it is still being initialized (e.g. battery powered devices).\n- (@floze-the-genius) Corrected roles for Gen 2+ input states. [#1498]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added option to ignore the timezone mismatch message (device timezone differs from the ioBroker host timezone).\n- (mcm1957) dependencies have been updated","tree":{"sha":"c3f2417d8b906eade3c1bf4fe2d38f407b449a2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/trees/c3f2417d8b906eade3c1bf4fe2d38f407b449a2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/commits/84462479f0762ac79a87103f2f08adfa55338b8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/84462479f0762ac79a87103f2f08adfa55338b8d","node_id":"C_kwDOCMaeW9oAKDg0NDYyNDc5ZjA3NjJhYzc5YTg3MTAzZjJmMDhhZGZhNTUzMzhiOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/f728c929368e759d973ab5338e39c3c142391a0a","sha":"f728c929368e759d973ab5338e39c3c142391a0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/f728c929368e759d973ab5338e39c3c142391a0a"}],"sha":"84462479f0762ac79a87103f2f08adfa55338b8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/84462479f0762ac79a87103f2f08adfa55338b8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/f728c929368e759d973ab5338e39c3c142391a0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T08:13:35Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T08:13:35Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"message":"prepare release 12.0.0","tree":{"sha":"139e066330d1e5f7bd45f135e0ab4d6b8d83e16d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/trees/139e066330d1e5f7bd45f135e0ab4d6b8d83e16d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/commits/f728c929368e759d973ab5338e39c3c142391a0a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/f728c929368e759d973ab5338e39c3c142391a0a","node_id":"C_kwDOCMaeW9oAKGY3MjhjOTI5MzY4ZTc1OWQ5NzNhYjUzMzhlMzljM2MxNDIzOTFhMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/378fb81eacf96ee540093b4df4dc1bfd8a11c16e","sha":"378fb81eacf96ee540093b4df4dc1bfd8a11c16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/378fb81eacf96ee540093b4df4dc1bfd8a11c16e"}],"sha":"f728c929368e759d973ab5338e39c3c142391a0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/f728c929368e759d973ab5338e39c3c142391a0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/378fb81eacf96ee540093b4df4dc1bfd8a11c16e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T16:26:25Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T16:26:25Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"message":"chore: release v12.0.0-alpha.11\n\n- (@mcm1957) **BREAKING:** Adapter requires node.js >= 22, js-controller >= 7.7.2 and admin >= 8.0.11 now.\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed MQTT commands getting lost with \"mqtt prefix was not set\" if they were sent while a device was (re)connecting.\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed inverted Relay0.Switch state of Shelly 1L Gen3 (shelly1lg3), Shelly 1PM Mini Gen3 (shelly1pmminig3), Shelly Pro 2PM (shellypro2pm) and Shelly Plug S Gen3 (shellyplugsg3) caused by a device firmware bug. [#1318]\n- (@mcm1957) Added a \"BLE Map\" button to the device manager toolbar which opens the Bluetooth map.\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly 1L Gen4 (shelly1lg4) and Shelly 2L Gen4 (shelly2lg4).\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed duplicated \"Total\" prefix in the device manager labels of the Shelly 3EM (SHEM-3) total values.\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed date states (timer/transition/boost start times) to report the timestamp in milliseconds so it is compatible with JavaScript Date handling.\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed authentication with Gen2+ devices running firmware 2.x which could fail with \"Wrong http username or http password!\" although the credentials were correct. [#1543]\n- (@mcm1957) Added experimental support for FrankEver Smart Sprinkler Controller (irrigation). [#1207]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Neo Smart Water Valve NAS-WV02W (neowatervalve). [#1322]\n- (@mcm1957) Added missing translations for the adapter configuration. [#1586]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed that the adapter needlessly rewrote object definitions on every device update and reconnect, which caused repeated object change events and log spam in other adapters (e.g. valuetrackerovertime). [#1560]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added a new \"Bluetooth map\" tab to the adapter configuration which shows which Bluetooth devices are received by which Shelly gateway, including the signal strength. The gateways are arranged in a circle and each device is shown at the gateway which receives it best - all other connections and the signal values can be switched on.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The device manager now updates the device list after renaming a device, after a firmware update and after installing the BLE gateway script - the cards showed outdated values before.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The device tiles now show when a device was last seen, and a device which goes offline is marked as disconnected immediately instead of only after reloading the list.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The BLE gateway script can now be installed and updated from the device manager - per device or for all devices which already have it installed. The installed script version is shown in the device details.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The list of gateways which receive a Bluetooth device (state \"receivedBy\") now collects all gateways instead of showing only the receivers of the last message. A gateway which stops receiving a device is removed after one hour.\n- (@GermanBluefox) Corrected wrong datapoint translations in all supported languages, e.g. current, voltage and apparent power.\n- (@patricknitsch) Device Manager now automatically shows power values on the device tile, and voltage, current, energy and frequency in the device info, for any device that reports them.\n- (@mcm1957) Added the missing translations for all datapoint names in all supported languages.\n- (@mcm1957) Added tests to validate that all datapoint names and descriptions are translated and that all i18n language files are consistent.\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Duo Bulb E27 Gen 3 (shellyduobulbg3). [#1385]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Multicolor Bulb E27 Gen 3 (shellycolorblbg3). [#1386]\n- (@mcm1957) The transition time can now be written for Shelly Dimmer1/Dimmer2 and for Gen2+ dimmers/lights (incl. Dimmer Gen3 and Dimmer Gen4). [#1214][#1224]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Top AC Portable EV Charger (topacportableevcharger) - **EXPERIMENTAL ONLY** [#1401]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Flood S Gen 4 (shellyfloodsg4). [#1380]\n- (@mcm1957) Added monophase mode support for Shelly 3EM G3 (shelly3em63g3). [#1540]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added option to ignore the timezone mismatch message (device timezone differs from the ioBroker host timezone).\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed MQTT errors (\"Cannot read properties of undefined\") if a device closes the connection while it is still being initialized (e.g. battery powered devices).\n- (@floze-the-genius) Corrected roles for Gen 2+ input states. [#1498]\n- (@klein0r) Updated ble script (v1.4) for Shelly firmware > 2.0\n- (@GermanBluefox) Codebase has been migrated to typescript.","tree":{"sha":"fc4c3fe7650b7c4081f7f8e9336338103f77b03a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/trees/fc4c3fe7650b7c4081f7f8e9336338103f77b03a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/commits/378fb81eacf96ee540093b4df4dc1bfd8a11c16e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","org