github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/5595c779a2868ffdd95f4c15621d6c212e6a31f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:39:43Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:39:43Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"message":"chore: release v12.0.0-alpha.9\n\n- (@mcm1957) **BREAKING:** Adapter requires node.js >= 22, js-controller >= 7.7.2 and admin >= 8.0.11 now.\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed inverted Relay0.Switch state of the Shelly 1L Gen3 (shelly1lg3) caused by a device firmware bug. [#1318]\n- (@mcm1957) Added a \"BLE Map\" button to the device manager toolbar which opens the Bluetooth map.\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly 1L Gen4 (shelly1lg4) and Shelly 2L Gen4 (shelly2lg4).\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed duplicated \"Total\" prefix in the device manager labels of the Shelly 3EM (SHEM-3) total values.\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed date states (timer/transition/boost start times) to report the timestamp in milliseconds so it is compatible with JavaScript Date handling.\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed authentication with Gen2+ devices running firmware 2.x which could fail with \"Wrong http username or http password!\" although the credentials were correct. [#1543]\n- (@mcm1957) Added experimental support for FrankEver Smart Sprinkler Controller (irrigation). [#1207]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Neo Smart Water Valve NAS-WV02W (neowatervalve). [#1322]\n- (@mcm1957) Added missing translations for the adapter configuration. [#1586]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed that the adapter needlessly rewrote object definitions on every device update and reconnect, which caused repeated object change events and log spam in other adapters (e.g. valuetrackerovertime). [#1560]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added a new \"Bluetooth map\" tab to the adapter configuration which shows which Bluetooth devices are received by which Shelly gateway, including the signal strength. The gateways are arranged in a circle and each device is shown at the gateway which receives it best - all other connections and the signal values can be switched on.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The device manager now updates the device list after renaming a device, after a firmware update and after installing the BLE gateway script - the cards showed outdated values before.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The device tiles now show when a device was last seen, and a device which goes offline is marked as disconnected immediately instead of only after reloading the list.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The BLE gateway script can now be installed and updated from the device manager - per device or for all devices which already have it installed. The installed script version is shown in the device details.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The list of gateways which receive a Bluetooth device (state \"receivedBy\") now collects all gateways instead of showing only the receivers of the last message. A gateway which stops receiving a device is removed after one hour.\n- (@GermanBluefox) Corrected wrong datapoint translations in all supported languages, e.g. current, voltage and apparent power.\n- (@patricknitsch) Device Manager now automatically shows power values on the device tile, and voltage, current, energy and frequency in the device info, for any device that reports them.\n- (@mcm1957) Added the missing translations for all datapoint names in all supported languages.\n- (@mcm1957) Added tests to validate that all datapoint names and descriptions are translated and that all i18n language files are consistent.\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Duo Bulb E27 Gen 3 (shellyduobulbg3). [#1385]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Multicolor Bulb E27 Gen 3 (shellycolorblbg3). [#1386]\n- (@mcm1957) The transition time can now be written for Shelly Dimmer1/Dimmer2 and for Gen2+ dimmers/lights (incl. Dimmer Gen3 and Dimmer Gen4). [#1214][#1224]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Top AC Portable EV Charger (topacportableevcharger) - **EXPERIMENTAL ONLY** [#1401]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Flood S Gen 4 (shellyfloodsg4). [#1380]\n- (@mcm1957) Added monophase mode support for Shelly 3EM G3 (shelly3em63g3). [#1540]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added option to ignore the timezone mismatch message (device timezone differs from the ioBroker host timezone).\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed MQTT errors (\"Cannot read properties of undefined\") if a device closes the connection while it is still being initialized (e.g. battery powered devices).\n- (@floze-the-genius) Corrected roles for Gen 2+ input states. [#1498]\n- (@klein0r) Updated ble script (v1.4) for Shelly firmware > 2.0\n- (@GermanBluefox) Codebase has been migrated to typescript.","tree":{"sha":"80b2668f0d946ae82255fc861d8ccabcddcf1a4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/trees/80b2668f0d946ae82255fc861d8ccabcddcf1a4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/commits/5595c779a2868ffdd95f4c15621d6c212e6a31f6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/5595c779a2868ffdd95f4c15621d6c212e6a31f6","node_id":"C_kwDOCMaeW9oAKDU1OTVjNzc5YTI4NjhmZmRkOTVmNGMxNTYyMWQ2YzIxMmU2YTMxZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/729c374ac28b5a08febe5524a1d6ac28297953f0","sha":"729c374ac28b5a08febe5524a1d6ac28297953f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/729c374ac28b5a08febe5524a1d6ac28297953f0"}],"sha":"5595c779a2868ffdd95f4c15621d6c212e6a31f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/5595c779a2868ffdd95f4c15621d6c212e6a31f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/729c374ac28b5a08febe5524a1d6ac28297953f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:31:21Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:31:21Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"message":"new release","tree":{"sha":"56707bd681bdcae1c82ddc71146ecf19eebab106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/trees/56707bd681bdcae1c82ddc71146ecf19eebab106"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/commits/729c374ac28b5a08febe5524a1d6ac28297953f0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/729c374ac28b5a08febe5524a1d6ac28297953f0","node_id":"C_kwDOCMaeW9oAKDcyOWMzNzRhYzI4YjVhMDhmZWJlNTUyNGExZDZhYzI4Mjk3OTUzZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/b2e716ff50fbfa4f22646b6e347cc53f8493af9a","sha":"b2e716ff50fbfa4f22646b6e347cc53f8493af9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/b2e716ff50fbfa4f22646b6e347cc53f8493af9a"}],"sha":"729c374ac28b5a08febe5524a1d6ac28297953f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/729c374ac28b5a08febe5524a1d6ac28297953f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/b2e716ff50fbfa4f22646b6e347cc53f8493af9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:24:56Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:24:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix inverted Relay0.Switch of Shelly 1L Gen3 (refers to #1318) (#1606)\n\n* Fix inverted Relay0.Switch of Shelly 1L Gen3 (refers to #1318)\n\nThe Shelly 1L Gen3 firmware publishes the switch output INVERTED on the\nstatus/switch:0 MQTT topic after a state change, while the events/rpc\nNotifyStatus message carries the correct value. Derive Relay0.Switch from\nNotifyStatus instead and add an http_publish (Switch.GetStatus) to reseed\nthe correct value on connect and at the regular poll interval.\n\nRelax the base.ts poll guard so an MQTT state may carry both mqtt_publish\nand http_publish; scoped to mqtt so the CoAP behaviour is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Move shelly1lg3 status hotfix into reusable gen2-hotfixes module (refers to #1318)\n\nExtract the MQTT outdated/inverted switch status workaround into a new\ngen2-hotfixes.ts module as fixMqttOutdatedSwitchStatus() so the same fix can\nbe reused for other affected devices without code duplication. shelly1lg3.ts\nnow calls this function instead of overriding the state inline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"05cd78798148dec11e1214227e9fe3a6fd2bad95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/trees/05cd78798148dec11e1214227e9fe3a6fd2bad95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/commits/b2e716ff50fbfa4f22646b6e347cc53f8493af9a","verification":{"payload":"tree 05cd78798148dec11e1214227e9fe3a6fd2bad95\nparent f4255fb5f8052e92d2c8a58374c155d93a21c6e1\nauthor Martin M. <mcm57@gmx.at> 1789745096 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789745096 +0200\n\nFix inverted Relay0.Switch of Shelly 1L Gen3 (refers to #1318) (#1606)\n\n* Fix inverted Relay0.Switch of Shelly 1L Gen3 (refers to #1318)\n\nThe Shelly 1L Gen3 firmware publishes the switch output INVERTED on the\nstatus/switch:0 MQTT topic after a state change, while the events/rpc\nNotifyStatus message carries the correct value. Derive Relay0.Switch from\nNotifyStatus instead and add an http_publish (Switch.GetStatus) to reseed\nthe correct value on connect and at the regular poll interval.\n\nRelax the base.ts poll guard so an MQTT state may carry both mqtt_publish\nand http_publish; scoped to mqtt so the CoAP behaviour is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Move shelly1lg3 status hotfix into reusable gen2-hotfixes module (refers to #1318)\n\nExtract the MQTT outdated/inverted switch status workaround into a new\ngen2-hotfixes.ts module as fixMqttOutdatedSwitchStatus() so the same fix can\nbe reused for other affected devices without code duplication. shelly1lg3.ts\nnow calls this function instead of overriding the state inline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrVfICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEnwQADLZrZKPQS8apEfBdbNJQERt\nP1YjIf72JisPuEpXhQ9FjL6vlogl7scVKrPJUsQWrSNyVUFH2OP7f6nQw862VVcv\n7pFMaF04jeVPyRVoO8F8jobeYS9xfsAyf2+Ws9gMp3plIPyfsfvpk1c8LzQxsWSO\nlzEIcfmd17dfCX2PzH4pUMaIPTaWLs589Rel3YH4rlZFX6SsVnLa9PdJwg51i2WM\n7FTIyIGEoQHs5ZV9umDUT0mRoN+w8wGVlZoELCvkOEsceViLfhhMNddYMrCkFctV\nqeC8eGr8UzmnfxowatRO/Jb94urLKmKOX/Q/ePPJxJIDDkIo2qytTchQZ6uWUhuC\nEL3q4t4si9jJPTmfHLs8n8M1DWtQuoaf/bxZlCpdmUiUj9CVzqxuA2RFbxKO2bcO\n4VBqMDKzGLplCDsiCkVLUGFI+GoxlEQl/d2mnLw+RA9haSAaprcQlSFYtPFHz6X4\nS2FE9c7jMJVF6O0/A2I2j8hJSE0VL+5FwrFst/z/zJH3KmsNetdb8V4yQbELA6kn\nYOSmzvHB+mopkX/pFyZD0KFXDzN0Gzbooz3a6KwNPxSqbLg5UdjLGs32NXxNd0Ip\nHFSL4hSaKRwZ9GYEh2cVCBAV6fRqICFjGiO6O6tN/rNXixBhaOPgZDvCKKO4/guK\ntn909y88yUNUU5AkRC8p\n=+WDT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T15:24:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/b2e716ff50fbfa4f22646b6e347cc53f8493af9a","node_id":"C_kwDOCMaeW9oAKGIyZTcxNmZmNTBmYmZhNGYyMjY0NmI2ZTM0N2NjNTNmODQ5M2FmOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commit/f4255fb5f8052e92d2c8a58374c155d93a21c6e1","sha":"f4255fb5f8052e92d2c8a58374c155d93a21c6e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/f4255fb5f8052e92d2c8a58374c155d93a21c6e1"}],"sha":"b2e716ff50fbfa4f22646b6e347cc53f8493af9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/b2e716ff50fbfa4f22646b6e347cc53f8493af9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/commits/f4255fb5f8052e92d2c8a58374c155d93a21c6e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T08:41:10Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T08:41:10Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"message":"chore: release v12.0.0-alpha.8\n\n- (@mcm1957) **BREAKING:** Adapter requires node.js >= 22, js-controller >= 7.7.2 and admin >= 8.0.11 now.\n- (@mcm1957) Added a \"BLE Map\" button to the device manager toolbar which opens the Bluetooth map.\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly 1L Gen4 (shelly1lg4) and Shelly 2L Gen4 (shelly2lg4).\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed duplicated \"Total\" prefix in the device manager labels of the Shelly 3EM (SHEM-3) total values.\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed date states (timer/transition/boost start times) to report the timestamp in milliseconds so it is compatible with JavaScript Date handling.\n- (@mcm1957) Fixed authentication with Gen2+ devices running firmware 2.x which could fail with \"Wrong http username or http password!\" although the credentials were correct. [#1543]\n- (@mcm1957) Added experimental support for FrankEver Smart Sprinkler Controller (irrigation). [#1207]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Neo Smart Water Valve NAS-WV02W (neowatervalve). [#1322]\n- (@mcm1957) Added missing translations for the adapter configuration. [#1586]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed that the adapter needlessly rewrote object definitions on every device update and reconnect, which caused repeated object change events and log spam in other adapters (e.g. valuetrackerovertime). [#1560]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added a new \"Bluetooth map\" tab to the adapter configuration which shows which Bluetooth devices are received by which Shelly gateway, including the signal strength. The gateways are arranged in a circle and each device is shown at the gateway which receives it best - all other connections and the signal values can be switched on.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The device manager now updates the device list after renaming a device, after a firmware update and after installing the BLE gateway script - the cards showed outdated values before.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The device tiles now show when a device was last seen, and a device which goes offline is marked as disconnected immediately instead of only after reloading the list.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The BLE gateway script can now be installed and updated from the device manager - per device or for all devices which already have it installed. The installed script version is shown in the device details.\n- (@GermanBluefox) The list of gateways which receive a Bluetooth device (state \"receivedBy\") now collects all gateways instead of showing only the receivers of the last message. A gateway which stops receiving a device is removed after one hour.\n- (@GermanBluefox) Corrected wrong datapoint translations in all supported languages, e.g. current, voltage and apparent power.\n- (@patricknitsch) Device Manager now automatically shows power values on the device tile, and voltage, current, energy and frequency in the device info, for any device that reports them.\n- (@mcm1957) Added the missing translations for all datapoint names in all supported languages.\n- (@mcm1957) Added tests to validate that all datapoint names and descriptions are translated and that all i18n language files are consistent.\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Duo Bulb E27 Gen 3 (shellyduobulbg3). [#1385]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Multicolor Bulb E27 Gen 3 (shellycolorblbg3). [#1386]\n- (@mcm1957) The transition time can now be written for Shelly Dimmer1/Dimmer2 and for Gen2+ dimmers/lights (incl. Dimmer Gen3 and Dimmer Gen4). [#1214][#1224]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Top AC Portable EV Charger (topacportableevcharger) - **EXPERIMENTAL ONLY** [#1401]\n- (@mcm1957) Added support for Shelly Flood S Gen 4 (shellyfloodsg4). [#1380]\n- (@mcm1957) Added monophase mode support for Shelly 3EM G3 (shelly3em63g3). [#1540]\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added option to ignore the timezone mismatch message (device timezone differs from the ioBroker host timezone).\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed MQTT errors (\"Cannot read properties of undefined\") if a device closes the connection while it is still being initialized (e.g. battery powered devices).\n- (@floze-the-genius) Corrected roles for Gen 2+ input states. [#1498]\n- (@klein0r) Updated ble script (v1.4) for Shelly firmware > 2.0\n- (@GermanBluefox) Codebase has been migrated to typescript.","tree":{"sha":"c038dbdc1d66e14a4a2eb8360f7b3707c27cc93f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/trees/c038dbdc1d66e14a4a2eb8360f7b3707c27cc93f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.shelly/git/commits/f4255fb5f8052e92d2c8a58374c155d93a21c6e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","receive