"type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/commits/40a05620049c6dfe8f7527b1f5abaf507daa3fca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T07:31:04Z","email":"d.krestov@creatio.com","name":"d-krestov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T07:31:04Z","email":"d.krestov@creatio.com","name":"d-krestov"},"message":"#ENG-102112 Review fixes (antonChernovCreatio): fallback scope, modify blocks, prompts, e2e cleanup\n\n- list-user-tasks: the \"update rather than fall back\" advice is scoped to the two page\n  tasks again; Send email and Approval keep the generic-userTask fallback an older\n  package builds.\n- modify-business-process addElement lists openEditPage? next to preconfiguredPage?,\n  each block qualified by its element type; paid for by merging the four per-block\n  entries (35016 bytes, re-measured in the budget comment).\n- The modify prompt and the create prompt''s step (1) - and the create description''s\n  list-user-tasks pointer - carve out PreconfiguredPageUserTask / OpenEditPageUserTask.\n- e2e: both refusal tests clean up in finally (create only when a regression left the\n  process), are Ignored with a reason when clio''s convergence check says the sandbox\n  package is behind, and the create fixture extracts tool text through one helper.\n  DeleteProcessAsync moved to Support/Mcp/ProcessDesignerE2ESupport for both fixtures.\n- ListUserTasks unit test pins the whole refusal phrase instead of a bare word.\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&(Module=McpServer|Module=Common)\" (8445 passed);\nboth e2e refusal tests green on net8.0 and net10.0 against a 1.6.6.88 stand, nothing left behind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4a0762b544ff0a3130eed6d4d588b0b3905fd82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundatio