m/users/d-krestov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/commits/7da247c165e658353cb013a936f9d6be90f3fc61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T06:58:53Z","email":"d.krestov@creatio.com","name":"d-krestov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T06:58:53Z","email":"d.krestov@creatio.com","name":"d-krestov"},"message":"#ENG-102112 Gate-3 fixes: list-user-tasks fallback, prompt carve-out, stale numbers\n\n- list-user-tasks: an environment that rejects a dedicated type is told to update\n  with install-process-builder, not to fall back to a generic userTask that cannot\n  carry the block; the version provenance is gone from this description and from\n  create-business-process (convergence makes the older-package clause unreachable,\n  and a number cannot express the capability across two package lines).\n- The list-user-tasks prompt carves out PreconfiguredPageUserTask and\n  OpenEditPageUserTask, matching its tool (unit test added).\n- Stale numbers re-measured: the get-tool-contract budget comment (modify 35047,\n  create 34745, describe 33367) and the cut paragraph of the bundle pins.\n- e2e: version precondition 1.6.6.88, the modify refusal also checks the element name.\n\nReview: gate 3 (three lenses) - no Blocker/High; these are its Medium/Low items in\nthis PR''s scope. Out of scope (pre-existing Open edit page wording) goes to ENG-102537.\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&(Module=McpServer|Module=Common)\" (8445 passed);\nthe two e2e refusal tests green on net8.0 and net10.0 against a 1.6.6.88 stand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"979d6204290e9783c12b201f009076e96705c668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/git/trees/979d6204290e9783c12b201f009076e96705c668"},"url":"htt