a64698f1b93655e59f988b0d6bf582","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/commits/5770acc43da64698f1b93655e59f988b0d6bf582"}],"sha":"d7880cb33bef6a721fe78ebc636427c98e216cc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/commits/d7880cb33bef6a721fe78ebc636427c98e216cc0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180284958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/d-krestov","id":180284958,"login":"d-krestov","node_id":"U_kgDOCr7uHg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-krestov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/commits/7ab76575b2254d755ba27657b7f53f4aff3ba0de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:25:56Z","email":"d.krestov@creatio.com","name":"d-krestov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:25:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ENG-100153 O5: accept an object for create-business-process ''descriptor'' (#1691)\n\n* #ENG-100153 Accept the process descriptor and operations as JSON values, keeping the string form\n\ncreate-business-process bound `descriptor` as a string, so the natural call - the descriptor as a JSON\nobject - was refused by the binder before the tool ran, and an agent serialized, escaped and\nre-checked the document through a shell to hand over a value it already held. The two modify tools\nhad the same shape for `operations`.\n\nAll three now bind the argument as JsonElement and read it through\nMcpToolArgumentSupport.TryReadJsonDocumentArgument: a value of the right kind is forwarded as its\nraw JSON text, a string is forwarded verbatim (byte-identical to before), anything else is refused\nnaming both accepted forms. modify-business-process-as-new-version keeps absent/null/empty as the\nsnapshot form, and its operations moved to an init property: the SDK emits an optional positional\nJsonElement? as {\"default\":null} and drops the description (measured; knowledge record added).\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&Module=McpServer\"\n(5749 passed); clio.mcp.e2e hermetic binder tests (net8.0 + net10.0) and the live object-descriptor\nbuild against a .NET Framework stand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Review fixes: type the JSON-document argument as \"any\", and prove the reader, not only the binder\n\n- The derived contract reported a typeless (any-JSON-value) member as \"object\", which described the\n  operations ARRAY as an object; McpToolRegistrySchemaContract now reports \"any\" for a schema that\n  constrains nothing, and a test pins it on all three process write tools.\n- The wrong-kind refusal says \"a JSON boolean\", not \"a JSON true\"; a non-container expectedKind throws.\n- One IsAbsentJsonDocument predicate replaces the copy in ModifyProcessAsNewVersionTool.\n- The modify e2e tests used a blank environment, which the target guard answers BEFORE the operations\n  reader runs; they now use an unregistered environment and pair the array with an object the reader\n  must refuse, so they prove the array was read.\n- NotBeNull guards before every CapturedOptions dereference; the unused JsonArgument.Value is gone;\n  the knowledge record states the new \"any\" type and drops an unrelated applies-to path.\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&Module=McpServer\"\n(5753 passed); clio.mcp.e2e no-stand ENG-100153 tests (4 passed, net10.0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Read the full contract in the derived-type test, so a fitted default lookup cannot cut the field under test\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"FullyQualifiedName~ProcessDesignerEmittedSchemaTests\" (15 passed).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Make the array half of the modify e2e tests assert what happened, not only what did not\n\nReview follow-up: the array call asserted only the ABSENCE of two refusals, so a reader that refused\nan array as missing (or threw) would have stayed green. It now asserts the call got as far as\nresolving the environment - the step after the reader - by the unregistered name, which carries a\nGUID so it can never meet a real one. Also: a whitespace-only operations string joins the snapshot\ncases, and the non-container expectedKind guard is pinned.\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&Module=McpServer\";\nclio.mcp.e2e no-stand ENG-100153 tests (4 passed, net8.0 and net10.0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Adapt the two ENG-92711 tests master added to the JsonElement arguments\n\nMaster added the compile-not-required-note tests for create- and modify-business-process (ENG-92711)\nafter this branch was cut. They build the args record with a raw string, which no longer compiles once\ndescriptor and operations bind as JsonElement; wrap them in JsonArgument.Text like every other\ndirect-construction call site in these fixtures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Review fixes: exit code 1 for a document of the wrong kind\n\n- A descriptor or operations of the wrong kind is a caller error, so it is answered with\n  FromValidationError (exit 1), the code the command gives the same mistake in string form. The\n  missing-document refusal keeps -1, which ENG-99100 tracks for the whole family.\n- A string argument is read once, and a string that cannot be read as text (an unpaired surrogate\n  escape) gets that refusal instead of GetString throwing out of the tool.\n- The reader''s docs state that it is only for arguments whose string form already was the contract.\n- Unit tests pin exit code 1 for the wrong-kind refusals of all three tools and cover the unreadable\n  string. The e2e wrong-kind tests assert the exit code over the real server, and the e2e object-form\n  build asserts what the string-form build does (no error, compile-not-required note).\n- Two stale <param> tags are dropped, AnnotationKeywords moves to the fields, and the knowledge record\n  names the SDK version it was measured on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Review fixes: package-name slot, fallback contract type, missing-document exit code\n\n- ModifyProcessAsNewVersionArgs.PackageName is an init property, like Operations. Kept positional, it\n  slid into the fourth slot the operations string used to hold, so new(env, name, uid, operationsJson)\n  still compiled and saved the version into a package named after a JSON array; that call no longer\n  compiles. The wire contract is unchanged, and a binder-level test pins that package-name still binds.\n- McpToolSchemaCatalog.MapClrType maps JsonElement to \"any\", so the reflection fallback get-tool-contract\n  uses without an invoker registry agrees with the registry-derived contract instead of answering \"object\".\n- A missing descriptor or operations (absent, null, or an empty or whitespace string) is refused with exit\n  code 1, like a document of the wrong kind, instead of -1, which tells the caller that clio broke. The\n  environment-name and process-identity checks keep -1 under ENG-99100.\n- Tests: the reflection fallback types all three arguments \"any\"; the missing-document refusal is pinned\n  through the real binder for all four spellings on both required arguments, and over the real MCP server\n  by one hermetic e2e call per tool; the two unit tests that pinned -1 now pin 1.\n- The knowledge record links method-parameter-tool-optionality-needs-a-default-and-a-reorder.md, drops a\n  type history that never shipped, and lists McpToolSchemaCatalog.cs and Directory.Packages.props.\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&Module=McpServer\" and \"TestCategory=Unit\";\ndotnet test clio.mcp.e2e on net10.0 and net8.0, filtered to the four process-designer fixtures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: n-torkvato <n.torkvato@creatio.com>","tree":{"sha":"823caf028185915f453a52c02292581592fb6504","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/git/trees/823caf028185915f453a52c02292581592fb6504"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/git/commits/7ab76575b2254d755ba27657b7f53f4aff3ba0de","verification":{"payload":"tree 823caf028185915f453a52c02292581592fb6504\nparent 35422fe4ce8716f069e4c1e389c8d67c9307e3b0\nauthor d-krestov <d.krestov@creatio.com> 1791383156 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791383156 +0300\n\nENG-100153 O5: accept an object for create-business-process ''descriptor'' (#1691)\n\n* #ENG-100153 Accept the process descriptor and operations as JSON values, keeping the string form\n\ncreate-business-process bound `descriptor` as a string, so the natural call - the descriptor as a JSON\nobject - was refused by the binder before the tool ran, and an agent serialized, escaped and\nre-checked the document through a shell to hand over a value it already held. The two modify tools\nhad the same shape for `operations`.\n\nAll three now bind the argument as JsonElement and read it through\nMcpToolArgumentSupport.TryReadJsonDocumentArgument: a value of the right kind is forwarded as its\nraw JSON text, a string is forwarded verbatim (byte-identical to before), anything else is refused\nnaming both accepted forms. modify-business-process-as-new-version keeps absent/null/empty as the\nsnapshot form, and its operations moved to an init property: the SDK emits an optional positional\nJsonElement? as {\"default\":null} and drops the description (measured; knowledge record added).\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&Module=McpServer\"\n(5749 passed); clio.mcp.e2e hermetic binder tests (net8.0 + net10.0) and the live object-descriptor\nbuild against a .NET Framework stand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Review fixes: type the JSON-document argument as \"any\", and prove the reader, not only the binder\n\n- The derived contract reported a typeless (any-JSON-value) member as \"object\", which described the\n  operations ARRAY as an object; McpToolRegistrySchemaContract now reports \"any\" for a schema that\n  constrains nothing, and a test pins it on all three process write tools.\n- The wrong-kind refusal says \"a JSON boolean\", not \"a JSON true\"; a non-container expectedKind throws.\n- One IsAbsentJsonDocument predicate replaces the copy in ModifyProcessAsNewVersionTool.\n- The modify e2e tests used a blank environment, which the target guard answers BEFORE the operations\n  reader runs; they now use an unregistered environment and pair the array with an object the reader\n  must refuse, so they prove the array was read.\n- NotBeNull guards before every CapturedOptions dereference; the unused JsonArgument.Value is gone;\n  the knowledge record states the new \"any\" type and drops an unrelated applies-to path.\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&Module=McpServer\"\n(5753 passed); clio.mcp.e2e no-stand ENG-100153 tests (4 passed, net10.0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Read the full contract in the derived-type test, so a fitted default lookup cannot cut the field under test\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"FullyQualifiedName~ProcessDesignerEmittedSchemaTests\" (15 passed).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Make the array half of the modify e2e tests assert what happened, not only what did not\n\nReview follow-up: the array call asserted only the ABSENCE of two refusals, so a reader that refused\nan array as missing (or threw) would have stayed green. It now asserts the call got as far as\nresolving the environment - the step after the reader - by the unregistered name, which carries a\nGUID so it can never meet a real one. Also: a whitespace-only operations string joins the snapshot\ncases, and the non-container expectedKind guard is pinned.\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&Module=McpServer\";\nclio.mcp.e2e no-stand ENG-100153 tests (4 passed, net8.0 and net10.0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Adapt the two ENG-92711 tests master added to the JsonElement arguments\n\nMaster added the compile-not-required-note tests for create- and modify-business-process (ENG-92711)\nafter this branch was cut. They build the args record with a raw string, which no longer compiles once\ndescriptor and operations bind as JsonElement; wrap them in JsonArgument.Text like every other\ndirect-construction call site in these fixtures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Review fixes: exit code 1 for a document of the wrong kind\n\n- A descriptor or operations of the wrong kind is a caller error, so it is answered with\n  FromValidationError (exit 1), the code the command gives the same mistake in string form. The\n  missing-document refusal keeps -1, which ENG-99100 tracks for the whole family.\n- A string argument is read once, and a string that cannot be read as text (an unpaired surrogate\n  escape) gets that refusal instead of GetString throwing out of the tool.\n- The reader''s docs state that it is only for arguments whose string form already was the contract.\n- Unit tests pin exit code 1 for the wrong-kind refusals of all three tools and cover the unreadable\n  string. The e2e wrong-kind tests assert the exit code over the real server, and the e2e object-form\n  build asserts what the string-form build does (no error, compile-not-required note).\n- Two stale <param> tags are dropped, AnnotationKeywords moves to the fields, and the knowledge record\n  names the SDK version it was measured on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* #ENG-100153 Review fixes: package-name slot, fallback contract type, missing-document exit code\n\n- ModifyProcessAsNewVersionArgs.PackageName is an init property, like Operations. Kept positional, it\n  slid into the fourth slot the operations string used to hold, so new(env, name, uid, operationsJson)\n  still compiled and saved the version into a package named after a JSON array; that call no longer\n  compiles. The wire contract is unchanged, and a binder-level test pins that package-name still binds.\n- McpToolSchemaCatalog.MapClrType maps JsonElement to \"any\", so the reflection fallback get-tool-contract\n  uses without an invoker registry agrees with the registry-derived contract instead of answering \"object\".\n- A missing descriptor or operations (absent, null, or an empty or whitespace string) is refused with exit\n  code 1, like a document of the wrong kind, instead of -1, which tells the caller that clio broke. The\n  environment-name and process-identity checks keep -1 under ENG-99100.\n- Tests: the reflection fallback types all three arguments \"any\"; the missing-document refusal is pinned\n  through the real binder for all four spellings on both required arguments, and over the real MCP server\n  by one hermetic e2e call per tool; the two unit tests that pinned -1 now pin 1.\n- The knowledge record links method-parameter-tool-optionality-needs-a-default-and-a-reorder.md, drops a\n  type history that never shipped, and lists McpToolSchemaCatalog.cs and Directory.Packages.props.\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&Module=McpServer\" and \"TestCategory=Unit\";\ndotnet test clio.mcp.e2e on net10.0 and net8.0, filtered to the four process-designer fixtures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: n-torkvato <n.torkvato@creatio.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxlZ0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA564QACRFJSjCflylRvVksxsaClpW\nljBu2xcvGtVXGJHv1SBczJWdCNACuo0xq50FuYrxpRkk6BsXRmnManDD2PfCxqQH\naNdH4euNl6uFBwNNis95CCAtgYd56UBGPPaI+Ec1IqWuB0luQwDyhePtkvJlgv1f\nqUGyK2xY7ajauyy4atGxDQDX2kRX0KChcGfX4MQzNctvG8dyPBAbvTLS2k8EdRFc\nrAm87rZZGzVIJ0I1AJQ31VWdBZaMhVLBRRyp3PzLkmuUvO9r5vQUV6OFuZJdZckC\nniEaBGrcJ5sS172oAeZBRwwNJasR6Qb02iiCEBYsngKES2MFHly+0CiwlIrS3ILa\nPDiEqNYlwA1jyTfY7gQHoMTGl5aIzXBO+2mWnltKmMcIhO7TC5OnQj0MHr8erV6B\n/TRRp0l3MCqfhUZIK3YOAFpTvON5ndJ03Acb+53Yq2ZSN72M1Q4D+J5qETxzGhwx\nw2+6HVRGRxanAB8fimB67ajA68xmY586EXNluGfodRXWqlzh20fa1Tf74bXcMW6r\nG4+Yr/HAdZhE6PJBhFobZsBof88NToJwmt/r9BiOjujfRD4T0qtV3wSwQBIekXp/\nx67vJbidJIssOB674su9ngBGhPbRhs9LSG5ys4EiKe9CWxpyrKjhR1Khl8AN5FiN\nsL9RYuyEq5fFSlAGjoUH\n=9lqa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T14:25:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following