ton.chernov@creatio.com","name":"Anton Chernov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T11:23:34Z","email":"anton.chernov@creatio.com","name":"Anton Chernov"},"message":"#ENG-100154 Carry repeated error codes once in an over-budget reply, guard the floor, stop over-claiming in the note\n\nReview (a-trofimchuk): the seven-contract reply had 45 bytes of headroom,\nand clio#1691 alone takes it 30 bytes over.\n\n- Fit first shares identical error-contract sets across the reply: a later\n  contract gets {codes: [], same-as: <first>}. The process-designer contracts\n  all carry the same generic codes, so this is lossless and frees ~1.5 KB\n  before any text is cut; fitting spends it keeping list-user-tasks whole.\n  A reply that fits, and any single-name lookup (describe-environment for\n  ClioRing), is unchanged.\n- The guard now measures the FLOOR - every contract short, codes shared -\n  which is 16 959 of 18 432 bytes (1 473 bytes headroom), and its message\n  names the largest kept form and says to trim it rather than raise the\n  budget.\n- The note says \"Marked sentences kept\" instead of \"Safety sentences kept\":\n  same length, and it no longer reads as \"nothing safety-relevant is missing\".\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj --filter \"(TestCategory=Unit&Module=McpServer)|FullyQualifiedName~McpE2eSelectionCoverageTests\" (6097 passed)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0592883dd5465a677c17f7953142b0d7ecfa353c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/git/trees/0592883dd5465a677c17f7953142b0d7ecfa353c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/git/commits/7dc0fd2282c132e1066cbb9f606ab7a5d3ca61fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/318628606?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anto