//api.github.com/users/d-krestov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/commits/6874cdd3621d3fbb42aaeef6758a76550b46ef27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:28:04Z","email":"d.krestov@creatio.com","name":"d-krestov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:28:04Z","email":"d.krestov@creatio.com","name":"d-krestov"},"message":"#ENG-102114 Bundle CrtProcessBuilder 1.6.6.79 (verification pass); the unresolved-reference wording says \"the remedy\" again; records say which dot\n\nBundles CrtProcessBuilder 1.6.6.79, packed from crt-process-builder commit 209246e6 (tag crtprocessbuilder-1.6.6.79;\nrestamp f377b6eb). It restores the filter''s private EnsureCanonicalSpelling, which the 1.6.6.78 rename had garbled; no\nbehaviour change. 1.6.6.78 was cut on this branch only and installed on one test stand; it was never published.\n\n- create/modify-business-process: an unresolvable reference \"names the reference and the remedy\" - for an unknown\n  element the refusal lists nothing, so \"what does exist\" was not true of every case.\n- Knowledge: the dot that draws the add-a-PROCESS-parameter advice is the one between [Element:] and [Parameter:];\n  the new record''s description scopes the check to the surfaces it covers.\n\nValidated: dotnet test clio.tests/clio.tests.csproj -f net10.0 --filter \"TestCategory=Unit&(Module=Common|Module=McpServer|Module=Core)\" (8695 passed);\nMetaPathConditionToolE2ETests 5/5 on net10.0 and net8.0 against 1.6.6.79 on d_krestov_n.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"968890f007e7ff8b0ccc02e64a47bd3bb6e8f334","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/git/trees/968890f007e7ff8b0ccc02e64a47bd3bb6e8f334"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Advance-Technologies-Foundation/clio/git/commits/6874cdd3621d3fbb42aaeef6758a76550b46ef27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned",