https://api.github.com/users/aferd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aferd/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aferd","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/sources-ui/commits/7b5928167220d4ae62311038e8fd082836b45c96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T15:40:51Z","email":"86322239+aferd@users.noreply.github.com","name":"alex"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T15:40:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(rbac): implement hybrid RBAC v1/v2 with Kessel SDK for integrations (#1485)\n\n* feat(rbac): implement hybrid RBAC v1/v2 with Kessel SDK for integrations\n\nImplements a hybrid approach to RBAC v2 migration:\n- Integrations permissions: Migrated to Kessel v2 (feature-flag based)\n- Sources permissions: Continue using Chrome API v1 (until service migration)\n\nThis allows v2 orgs to use Kessel for integrations while sources service\nremains on v1 RBAC, preventing permission failures when the\nplatform.rbac.workspaces feature flag is enabled.\n\nKey Changes:\n- Added @project-kessel/react-kessel-access-check dependency\n- Created Kessel integration layer (src/rbac/)\n- Updated PermissionsChecker to use hybrid permission loading\n- Wrapped app with Kessel providers in AppEntry\n- Migrated AppEntry.js and PermissionsChecker.js to TypeScript\n\nPermission Flow:\n- v1 orgs (flag OFF): All permissions via Chrome API\n- v2 orgs (flag ON): Integrations via Kessel, Sources via Chrome API\n\nImplementation follows notifications-frontend pattern with hybrid\napproach as sources service has not migrated to Kessel yet.\n\nRelated: insights-chrome PR #3559 (skip v1 RBAC for v2 orgs)\nCloses: RHCLOUD-47732\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(rbac): add comprehensive tests for hybrid RBAC implementation\n\nAdded 24 tests covering hybrid v1/v2 RBAC approach:\n\nPermissionsChecker Tests (13 tests):\n- v1 org: all permissions via Chrome API\n- v2 org: sources via Chrome, integrations via Kessel\n- Feature flag branching logic\n- Kessel loading state handling\n\nPermission Mapper Tests (5 tests):\n- Kessel v2 → Redux v1 state mapping\n- Integrations permissions mapping\n- Value preservation without conversion\n\nKessel Actions Tests (6 tests):\n- Redux action dispatching for integrations\n- Correct action types\n- Sources NOT dispatched (hybrid approach)\n\nTest Results:\n- 147 test suites passed\n- 1063 tests passed (4 skipped)\n- All new tests passing\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address code review findings\n\n- Add language tags to fenced code blocks in markdown files\n- Add blank lines around markdown tables (markdownlint compliance)\n- Fix TypeScript typing: replace any with proper thunk types\n- Add error propagation for Kessel permission check failures\n- Use ACTION_TYPES constants instead of string literals in tests\n- Update kesselActions.js reference to kesselActions.ts in docs\n\nAll tests passing (24/24 RBAC tests)\nBuild successful\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: exclude test files from TypeScript build\n\n- Add exclude pattern to tsconfig.json for test files\n- Re-add (ACTION_TYPES as any) cast for dynamically generated types\n- Prevents test-only Jest types from breaking production build\n\nBuild successful ✓\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve eslint linting errors\n\n- Add eslint-disable comments for necessary any types\n- Fix prettier formatting issues\n- Properly position eslint-disable on same line as ''as any'' casts\n\nLint passing: only 3 pre-existing warnings (console.log in Widget services)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6def6028dacdae3461631e200047f4851c9d4d60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/sources-ui/git/trees/6def6028dacdae3461631e200047f4851c9d4d60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/sources-ui/git/commits/7b5928167220d4ae62311038e8fd082836b45c96","verification":{"payload":"tree 6def6028dacdae3461631e200047f4851c9d4d60\nparent 17bc54387485ffe9f5af742d94a966bda741a40d\nauthor alex <86322239+aferd@users.noreply.github.com> 1781106051 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781106051 -0400\n\nfeat(rbac): implement hybrid RBAC v1/v2 with Kessel SDK for integrations (#1485)\n\n* feat(rbac): implement hybrid RBAC v1/v2 with Kessel SDK for integrations\n\nImplements a hybrid approach to RBAC v2 migration:\n- Integrations permissions: Migrated to Kessel v2 (feature-flag based)\n- Sources permissions: Continue using Chrome API v1 (until service migration)\n\nThis allows v2 orgs to use Kessel for integrations while sources service\nremains on v1 RBAC, preventing permission failures when the\nplatform.rbac.workspaces feature flag is enabled.\n\nKey Changes:\n- Added @project-kessel/react-kessel-access-check dependency\n- Created Kessel integration layer (src/rbac/)\n- Updated PermissionsChecker to use hybrid permission loading\n- Wrapped app with Kessel providers in AppEntry\n- Migrated AppEntry.js and PermissionsChecker.js to TypeScript\n\nPermission Flow:\n- v1 orgs (flag OFF): All permissions via Chrome API\n- v2 orgs (flag ON): Integrations via Kessel, Sources via Chrome API\n\nImplementation follows notifications-frontend pattern with hybrid\napproach as sources service has not migrated to Kessel yet.\n\nRelated: insights-chrome PR #3559 (skip v1 RBAC for v2 orgs)\nCloses: RHCLOUD-47732\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(rbac): add comprehensive tests for hybrid RBAC implementation\n\nAdded 24 tests covering hybrid v1/v2 RBAC approach:\n\nPermissionsChecker Tests (13 tests):\n- v1 org: all permissions via Chrome API\n- v2 org: sources via Chrome, integrations via Kessel\n- Feature flag branching logic\n- Kessel loading state handling\n\nPermission Mapper Tests (5 tests):\n- Kessel v2 → Redux v1 state mapping\n- Integrations permissions mapping\n- Value preservation without conversion\n\nKessel Actions Tests (6 tests):\n- Redux action dispatching for integrations\n- Correct action types\n- Sources NOT dispatched (hybrid approach)\n\nTest Results:\n- 147 test suites passed\n- 1063 tests passed (4 skipped)\n- All new tests passing\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address code review findings\n\n- Add language tags to fenced code blocks in markdown files\n- Add blank lines around markdown tables (markdownlint compliance)\n- Fix TypeScript typing: replace any with proper thunk types\n- Add error propagation for Kessel permission check failures\n- Use ACTION_TYPES constants instead of string literals in tests\n- Update kesselActions.js reference to kesselActions.ts in docs\n\nAll tests passing (24/24 RBAC tests)\nBuild successful\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: exclude test files from TypeScript build\n\n- Add exclude pattern to tsconfig.json for test files\n- Re-add (ACTION_TYPES as any) cast for dynamically generated types\n- Prevents test-only Jest types from breaking production build\n\nBuild successful ✓\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve eslint linting errors\n\n- Add eslint-disable comments for necessary any types\n- Fix prettier formatting issues\n- Properly position eslint-disable on same line as ''as any'' casts\n\nLint passing: only 3 pre-existing warnings (console.log in Widget services)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKYWDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAufQQABnyubviucXU4wH5KBdRZAxx\nr8hQ5OmXF//HNLP47zNYzID3WSBiWzBBDL8MACn3yzmcF4flxDp