e":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darsene","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ovh/manager/commits/b2e8c719732ec284ec6c11dad44913d1b5c5a5b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:27:23Z","email":"david.arsene.ext@ovhcloud.com","name":"David Arsène"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:46:03Z","email":"72250222+darsene@users.noreply.github.com","name":"darsene"},"message":"feat(dedicated.dbaas): retire legacy access management behind a flag\n\nEvery legacy write control on a non-IAM Logs Data Platform service is now gated on the\nlogs-data-platform:legacy-access-decommissioned availability flag: the password tile action, the\naccount-setup password mode, Add a token (button and route), Add a role, the row Edit entry, Add a\nmember, and the attach panes of the role permissions widget. Reads, deletes, revokes and detaches\nare untouched, and nothing is removed: before the date the interface is unchanged apart from an\ninformational notice.\n\nThe flag is read once, on the root state, and fails closed. A failed request, an unpublished key\nand the loading window all resolve to \"not decommissioned\", which keeps the legacy controls\navailable.\n\nresolves: #MAOBS-629\n\nSigned-off-by: David Arsène <david.arsene.ext@ovhcloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: CDS Translator Agent <opensource@ovh.net>","tree":{"sha":"0deb05058c5321a248d62ccafd4796621232e64d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ovh/manager/git/trees/0deb05058c5321a248d62ccafd4796621232e64d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ovh/manager/git/commits/b2e8c719732ec284ec6c11dad44913d1b5c5a5b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72250222?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darsene/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darsene/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.